      "Edit(scripts/loop-engineering/lib/**)",
      "Write(scripts/loop-engineering/lib/**)",
      "Edit(scripts/loop-engineering/run.mjs)",
      "Write(scripts/loop-engineering/run.mjs)",
      "Edit(AGENTIC_SECURITY_DIFFERENTIATION_PRD.md)",
      "Write(AGENTIC_SECURITY_DIFFERENTIATION_PRD.md)",
      "Edit(scripts/loop-engineering/profiles/**)",
      "Write(scripts/loop-engineering/profiles/**)",
      "Edit(scripts/loop-engineering/test/**)",
      "Write(scripts/loop-engineering/test/**)",
      "Edit(scripts/assurance-differentiation/test/**)",
      "Write(scripts/assurance-differentiation/test/**)"
    ],
    "honestLimits": [
      "Bash(node:*) can run arbitrary JavaScript, so the allow list scopes tool use but is not a filesystem sandbox. The controller re-verifies every attempt itself and the final phase re-runs all suites from scratch; worker claims and worker-written evidence are never trusted. Read confinement of verifier keys and sealed labels is the job of CORE-003, not of this profile.",
      "The installed Claude CLI has no --max-turns flag; the 80-turn cap is enforced externally by counting assistant turns in the stream and terminating the attempt.",
      "Edit/Write deny rules protect the controller, profile and protected suite wrappers from the worker tool surface only; a worker running node can still write any path the OS user can. Evidence signing and tree-digest staleness, not these rules, are what make tampering visible.",
      "Bash(rm:*) is denied outright: workers delete files with node or by overwriting."
    ],
    "protectedPaths": [
      ".loop-engineering/",
      "scripts/loop-engineering/",
      "scripts/assurance-differentiation/test/",
      "AGENTIC_SECURITY_DIFFERENTIATION_PRD.md"
    ]
  },
